# Renovate's Forgejo credential — plaintext TEMPLATE. The real file is
# nixos/renovate.sops.env, encrypted to the production age recipient.
#
# WHY THIS IS A .sops.env AND NOT A KEY IN secrets.sops.yaml
# ---------------------------------------------------------
# CLAUDE.md's rule is that OS-level secrets live in the flake's
# secrets.sops.yaml and are extracted per-key by sops-nix. That rule is right,
# and this file is a deliberate, narrow exception with one cause:
#
#   Adding a key to an ALREADY-ENCRYPTED sops-yaml requires the age PRIVATE
#   key, because sops has to recompute the file MAC over every value. Only
#   the key holder can do it. nixos/secrets.sops.yaml today holds two REAL
#   ed25519 private keys (BACKUP_VPS_SSH_KEY, BACKUP_STORAGEBOX_SSH_KEY —
#   411 and 419 plaintext bytes, not the ~35-byte changeme_ strings), so
#   "regenerate it from the .example and re-encrypt" would destroy them.
#
# Encryption, by contrast, needs only the PUBLIC key in .sops.yaml — so a new
# file can be created by anyone, which is what makes this shape work.
#
# The content is consumed WHOLE, as a systemd EnvironmentFile, by exactly one
# unit. That is the same criterion CLAUDE.md gives for the stack .sops.env
# files ("the sops CLI decrypts the whole file, which is exactly the artifact
# wanted"), so dotenv is not a compromise here — it is the right format.
#
# nixos/modules/ci-secrets.nix decrypts it at runtime into
# /run/ci-secrets/renovate.env with the host age key, exactly the way
# decrypt-sops-envs.service does for stacks.
#
# TO FILL IN (one operator step, on the live host or the desktop):
#
#   1. In Forgejo, as the user Renovate should act as:
#        Settings -> Applications -> Generate New Token
#      Scopes (Forgejo 16 token model): read:user, write:issue,
#      write:repository. Nothing more — Renovate opens PRs and reads repos.
#      🚨 This is a PAT and it is ONLY for Renovate's own API calls. It must
#      NEVER be used by a workflow to push: see the loop-prevention comment
#      in .forgejo/workflows/renovate-pins.yml.
#   2. sopsedit nixos/renovate.sops.env      # paste the token
#   3. nixos-rebuild switch --target-host idan@10.0.0.3 --use-remote-sudo \
#        --flake .#services-vm
#
# Until step 2 happens the value stays changeme_*, ci-secrets.nix refuses to
# write the runtime file, and renovate.service is SKIPPED by its
# ConditionPathExists (skipped, not failed — an unconfigured optional service
# must not page anyone).

# Forgejo personal access token for the Renovate bot user.
RENOVATE_TOKEN=changeme_forgejo_renovate_pat
